  abstract = {Record of our 3rd online gathering for the NSF SEEKCommons project. This year we invited our RCN members to hear from our newest cohort of Fellows, who will be reporting on their ongoing projects. Here is the list of presentations: Ana Trisovic, Researcher, Massachusetts Institute of Technology Project: High-Dimensional Geospatial Data Management with DataverseMentor: Jeff Ward (Animikii) Brianna Johns, Professional Practitioner, Digital Naturalism Lab in PanamaProject: Understanding the Socio-environmental Dynamics of Open Hardware in Wildlife Conservation EffortsMentor: Luis Felipe R. Murillo (University of Notre Dame) Keren Reichler, Ph.D. Candidate, Rice UniversityProject title: Supporting Transitions to Agroecology Through Open Science and Grassroots Technology Innovation in Mendoza, ArgentinaMentor: Daniel Mietchen (Leibniz Institute for Information Infrastructure) Uzoamaka Nwachukwu, Ph.D. Candidate, Indiana University BloomingtonProject title: Extracting Narratives: A Digital Analysis of Newspaper Reports on Mining in Eastern NigeriaMentor: Scott Frickel (Brown University) Raymar Hampshire, Professional Practitioner, University of MichiganProject: The Justice Narratives Library – A Student-Led Knowledge Commons for Socio-Environmental Case StudiesMentor: Lane Rasberry (University of Virginia) Cynthia Browne, Researcher, Max Planck Institute, Berlin, GermanyProject title: Radiant Lands: Commoning Knowledge on Exposure in the Navajo NationMentor: Sarah McCullough (University of California, Davis) Felipe Mamomoli Andrade, Professional Practitioner, Center for Information Technology - Renato Archer (CTI), Campinas, BrazilProject title: A Forest Made of Data: Mapping Knowledge Flows About Emissions Reduction in the Brazilian Amazon Mentor: Gerd Heber (HDF Group) Rohit Nagubandi, Tor Project Fellow, Graduate Student, University of California, Santa CruzProject tile: Green Onion: The Environmental Impacts of Open Source Mentor: Gustavo Gus (Tor Projec