  url = {http://www.scielo.cl/scielo.php?script=sci_arttext&pid=S0718-50492025000100234&lang=pt},
  abstract = {Abstract: This editorial introduces the special issue "Digital Capitalism, Big Tech and Education", which brings together twelve articles from Latin America and Europe examining the transformations driven by the platformization of education. Through critical perspectives, the contributions address educational privatization, data extractivism, algorithmic subjectivation, and the ethical tensions that emerge under digital capitalism. Alternatives such as care ethics, technological sovereignty, and feminist pedagogies are also explored. The issue aims to highlight these educational disputes from an international, interdisciplinary, and situated perspective, inviting readers to envision more just and democratic educational futures in the face of corporate power and the technologization of teaching.},
